# Initial Setup's Frame Type page for a copter older than 3.5, ported from
# GCSViews/ConfigurationView/ConfigFrameType.cs.
#
# InitialSetup lists that page for isCopter && gotAllParams && !isCopter35plus, and
# ConfigFrameClassType for a vehicle with FRAME_CLASS or a copter of 3.5 and later
# (InitialSetup.cs:184-192). SITL runs ArduCopter 4.6, which has FRAME_CLASS and FRAME_TYPE and no
# FRAME, so this script cannot show the page: what it proves is the list's choice - Mandatory
# Hardware opens on ConfigFrameClassType, straight after the heading, with no ConfigFrameType - and
# that the older page's object, never shown, has read nothing and written nothing, while the newer
# page is the one that opens. The page itself - Activate on FRAME, the six radio buttons with
# WinForms' events in the Designer's order, the pictures, the writes through the real link and
# "Set FRAME Failed" - is covered by the unit tests in
# crates/mp-gui/src/config/frame_type_legacy.rs, and the list's condition by setup.rs's
# the_vehicle_picks_the_frame_and_compass_pages, with a copter of 3.4.
#
# Needs SITL copter on tcp:127.0.0.1:5760 started from tools/sitl/params/copter.parm. Nothing is
# written. Run as
#
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/config-frametype-legacy.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760

screen params
window 1600x1200
settle 6

click param-download
settle 15
expect params.held > 1000
expect params.value.FRAME_CLASS 1

click tab-setup
settle 1
click setup-page-ConfigMandatory
settle 1
expect setup.page ConfigMandatory

# The list: a 4.6 copter gets the newer page, right after the heading, and not the older one.
expect setup.groups ~ Mandatory Hardware=ConfigFrameClassType,ConfigAccelerometerCalibration,
expect setup.shown ~ ConfigMandatory,ConfigFrameClassType,ConfigAccelerometerCalibration,

# The older page's object: never shown, so nothing read and nothing written.
expect config.framelegacy.active false
expect config.framelegacy.enabled true
expect config.framelegacy.read none
expect config.framelegacy.checked none
expect config.framelegacy.sent 0
expect config.framelegacy.pending 0
expect config.framelegacy.message none

# Frame Type opens the newer page; the older one stays as it was.
click setup-page-ConfigFrameClassType
settle 1
expect setup.page ConfigFrameClassType
expect setup.title Frame Type
expect config.frame.active true
expect config.framelegacy.active false
expect config.framelegacy.sent 0
